  "term": "ABCL",
  "definition": "ABCL refers to the Adult Behavior Checklist, an assessment form for adults aged 18 to 59 that gathers information from people who know the adult well. It is used alongside the Adult Self-Report to evaluate adult behavioral and emotional problems across settings, with scores compared to age- and sex-based norms.",
